    "done_when": "The paid-lane publisher must refresh a subscription account's window when its reading has gone stale, so Jev and preflight see the account as it is now.\n\nMeasured 2026-10-07:\n- after the codex account reset, budget preflight's account probe read codex, codex-astra and codex-luna at 0%;\n- ~/public/reckon/paid-lanes.json still published 85% for the seven-day window, observed at 01:26:39Z, from the newest rollout, marked stale;\n- python -m reckon.crew.paid_lanes --once, run every 5 min by reckon-paid-lanes.timer, marks a window stale after DEFAULT_STALE_SECONDS (1 h) but never refetches. Its codex source is the newest rollout, which ages whenever codex is idle;\n- budget.run_probe, used through preflight's probe_runner, already reads the account surface;\n- the claude account read fails with HTTP 403.\n\n1. When a subscription account's window is past its staleness horizon, the publisher refreshes that window through the existing account probe (budget.run_probe, or the preflight path that wraps it). Publish the probe's reading with source \"probe\" and its observed_at. Do not add a provider call path.\n2. Rate-limit it: at most one probe per account per staleness horizon, recorded durably so a crash or a restart cannot loop. A probe that fails, such as claude's 403, keeps the last reading with its age and stale flag and records the failure reason on the account entry.\n3. A probe reading that shows a reset (a seven-day utilisation lower than the stale reading, with resets_at moved forward) replaces the stale figure at once. reckon/crew/budget_reset.py, landing in the concurrent codex-banked-reset node, detects a consumed reset from consecutive readings; leave its logic alone, and just make sure the fresh reading is what it will see.\n4. Tests in tests/test_publisher_refreshes_stale_windows.py:\n   - a stale codex window with a stubbed probe is refreshed once and published with source probe;\n   - a second publish within the horizon does not probe again;\n   - a failing probe keeps the old reading, marked stale, with the reason;\n   - a fresh window is never probed.\n   Tests never call a live provider; the suite already stubs run_probe.\n5. After the change, run the publisher once by hand. Show the codex accounts' seven-day reading, source and age in the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/publisher-refreshes-stale-windows.html.\n\nGate: tests/test_paid_lanes*.py, tests/test_preflight_reads_the_published_document.py, tests/test_headroom_publishes_real_readings.py, tests/test_budget*.py and the new test file. Run them with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log for base and one for head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta.",
